// Installed Shortcut name: MAIN - Jelly Greeting Demo
// Purpose: Demonstrate an explicit input/result call to the reusable formatter.
// Role: Example main workflow
// Specification revision: 1 | Interface version: 1.0
// Input: Incoming content ignored; supplies literal Henry as one Text value.
// Output: One greeting Text from utility, expected Hello, Henry!.
// Direct execution: No prompt; no-recipient Respond displays final greeting.
// Called execution: Returns greeting; no intended extra display.
// Errors: Missing/incompatible utility or action failure may halt; no catch.
// Dependencies: UTIL - Jelly Format Greeting, interface 1.0,
//               util-jelly-format-greeting.jelly (same directory).
// External apps/services: None
// Side effects: Respond when no recipient; no files/network/clipboard changes.
// Permissions: No protected data access required by these actions.
// Target: iOS 26 provisional; Share Sheet/Siri/background contexts not specified.
// Candidate compiler: Open-Jellycore e1ec31c2ee192c8721749f9eb3b50108e38891cf
// Evidence: Syntax reviewed against docs/source; not compiled/imported/tested.
// References: ../docs/jellycuts-reference.md | Tests: ../tests/examples.md

import Shortcuts

var name = "Henry"
runShortcut(name: "UTIL - Jelly Format Greeting", input: name, show: false) >> greeting
output(result: "${greeting}", noResultBehavior: Respond, response: "${greeting}")
